## Images

**Every post must:**

- Reference a `thumbnail` path in frontmatter.
- Open the body with a `<figure>` block whose `src` is the **same path** as the `thumbnail`, before any prose. This is the lead image — it visually opens the post and is what shows up on listings.
- Optionally include additional inline `<figure>` blocks lower in the body when extra visuals genuinely help the argument. The lead figure is mandatory; further figures are content decisions, not a structural rule.

**Storage**: `public/content/posts/<slug>/<image-name>.png`. The path served at runtime is `/content/posts/<slug>/<image-name>.png`. Filenames are kebab-case and descriptive.

**Inline figure pattern** (use raw HTML, not Markdown image syntax):

```html
<figure>
  <img alt="Descriptive text good enough to be an image-generation prompt" src="/content/posts/<slug>/<image-name>.png" />
  <figcaption>Editorial caption that adds context, not a repeat of the alt.</figcaption>
</figure>
```

- `alt` must be detailed enough to use directly as an image generation prompt. Describe subjects, layout, style, colors, mood. The author generates images separately from this text.
- `figcaption` adds editorial commentary or framing for the image. It is read by humans; the alt is read by screen readers and image generators. They should not be identical.

**Lead figure placement**: the lead `<figure>` block goes **immediately after the closing `---` of the frontmatter**, with no prose between the frontmatter and the figure. The first paragraph of the post follows the figure.

**Image generation workflow**: The author writes the post with `<figure>` blocks pointing at `src` paths that don't yet exist. After the post draft is approved, the author generates images from the `alt` text and saves them at the suggested paths. The post text is the source for the prompts.

---

## Required closing section: Further reading

Every post must end with a **`## Further reading`** section that links to 1–3 other posts on the blog. The purpose is to weave the archive into a connected web rather than a flat list of posts.

- Recommendations must be **genuinely relevant** to the post's topic, not random or filler.
- It's fine to link both to older posts (2018-era) and to newer posts in the same series.
- Use Markdown links with the canonical post path:
  - EN: `[Post title](/YYYY/MM/DD/slug)`
  - PT: `[Título](/pt/YYYY/MM/DD/slug)`
- The PT version of a post links to PT versions of the recommended posts.

Format:

```markdown
## Further reading

- [Why every engineer should keep a journal](/2026/05/03/why-every-engineer-should-keep-a-journal)
- [From writing code to designing intelligence](/2026/04/14/from-writing-code-to-designing-intelligence)
```

---

## MDX vs MD

- Use `.md` by default.
- Use `.mdx` only when the post embeds Astro components (e.g. `<SankeyChart />`, `<Codepen />`, `<Animation />`). Don't reach for `.mdx` for plain `<figure>` blocks — those work in `.md` already.
